        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Site engineers considered heavy seasonal rainfall while preparing a capacity check for the ferry terminal sign. Passenger sight lines determine the sign installation height. The design must also be explained clearly in the safety briefing. A square-based pyramid has base side 10 cm and perpendicular height 15 cm. A second pyramid has the same volume but base side 5 cm. Find the second pyramid’s perpendicular height in cm."
        }
      ],
      "marks": 5,
      "primary_outcome": "5.6",
      "secondary_outcomes": [],
      "response": {
        "type": "numeric",
        "comparison_mode": "exact_numeric",
        "canonical_answer": "60",
        "canonical_latex": "60",
        "accepted_answers": [],
        "absolute_tolerance": null,
        "rounding_precision": null,
        "unit": null
      },
      "hints": [
        {
          "stage": 1,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Find the first volume, then keep it fixed for the second pyramid."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "stage": 2,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Because the base side is halved, its area is quartered, so the height must become four times as large."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "solution": [
        {
          "position": 1,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Select the relevant dimensions and apply the mensuration relationship."
            },
            {
              "type": "display_math",
              "latex": "V=\\frac13(10)^2(15)=500,\\quad 500=\\frac13(5)^2H\\Rightarrow H=60"
            }
          ],
          "mark_type": "M",
          "mark_value": 4
        },
        {
